        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:56:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64158,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 477,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Uterus, fallopian tubes, and ovaries</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:56:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64159,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 477,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Abnormal vaginal bleeding is the presenting symptom in more than half of cases. The preceding gestational event was normal pregnancy in more than half of cases, and a history of previous molar pregnancy is documented in about one&nbsp;third of cases. Serum hCG level is usually slightly elevated with mixed ETT and PSTT and slightly or moderately elevated with tumours that have a choriocarcinoma component. High levels of hCG are mainly observed in patients with lung metastasis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:56:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64160,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 477,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients are aged 15&ndash;60&nbsp;years (median: 34&nbsp;years) {12060455}. These tumours are very rare {29897391; 18227827; 26597227; 31206335}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:56:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64161,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 477,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:56:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64162,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 477,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The development of mixed trophoblastic tumour has been proposed to recapitulate the differentiation of trophoblast in early placenta. Cytotrophoblast, the presumed trophoblastic stem cell, undergoes neoplastic transformation along different lineages: into PSTT when it differentiates towards implantation-site intermediate trophoblast and into ETT when it differentiates towards chorionic-type intermediate trophoblast {18059230}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:56:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64163,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 477,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is a haemorrhagic mass lesion, with or without necrosis. Tumours not treated presurgically range from 2 to 8&nbsp;cm in size.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:56:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64164,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 477,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histopathology shows the presence of discrete areas of choriocarcinoma, PSTT, and/or ETT, with characteristic histomorphology of each subtype as described above. The most common mixed trophoblastic tumour is mixed choriocarcinoma and ETT; less common are mixed choriocarcinoma and PSTT and mixed ETT and PSTT {26261623; 29897391}. Least common is mixed choriocarcinoma, ETT, and PSTT, with only 2&nbsp;reported cases {9808132; 18227827}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:56:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64165,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 477,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Malignant trophoblastic cells may be seen in cervical cytology.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:56:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64166,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 477,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Genotyping distinguishes gestational from non-gestational tumours {28877059}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:56:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64167,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 477,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> distinctive morphological features of each subtype of gestational trophoblastic neoplasia, further supported by immunohistochemistry.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> genotyping.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:56:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64168,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 477,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "<p>The FIGO and Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM classifications are used for staging.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-23T12:29:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64169,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 477,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Data are limited because of the small number of cases. In one study, of the cases for which stage status was known, 50% were FIGO stage&nbsp;I and 37.5% were FIGO stage&nbsp;III (with lung metastasis). Mixed ETT and PSTT has the most indolent course {29897391}. Metastatic disease has been observed most commonly in cases with a choriocarcinoma component {9808132; 18227827}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:56:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]